        "original_id": "62065930-d91a-5392-a2e3-e33ff59679ba",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Ritter, Penny Marshall, Cassie Yates, Bert Convy, Constance McCashin, Tex Ritter, Jason Ritter, Tyler Ritter\n- Works: Love Thy Neighbor, Three's Company\n- Awards: Primetime Emmy Award, Golden Globe Award\n\nFacts:\n- Jonathan Southworth Ritter was born on September 17, 1948, and died on September 11, 2003, and he was an American actor and comedian.\n- John Ritter was the son of singer and actor Tex Ritter and the father of actors Jason Ritter and Tyler Ritter.\n- John Ritter was best known for playing Jack Tripper on the ABC sitcom Three's Company from 1977 to 1984.\n- In 1984, John Ritter received a Primetime Emmy Award and a Golden Globe Award for Three's Company.\n- Love Thy Neighbor is a 1984 American made-for-television romantic comedy film.\n- Love Thy Neighbor starred John Ritter, Penny Marshall, Cassie Yates, Bert Convy, and Constance McCashin.",
